<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ana Sagar Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Anasagar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ana Sagar is an artificial lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajmer">Ajmer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in the mid-12th century by the Chahamana king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnoraja">Arnoraja</a>, also called Anaji, after whom it is named, by damming a stream in the Aravalli hills. The Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jahangir">Jahangir</a> laid out the Daulat Bagh gardens beside it, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> added marble pavilions on its embankment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ana-sagar-lake.jpg" alt="Ana Sagar Lake" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fatehrawkey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Anas%C4%81gar_Lake_1_PHOTOGRAPHED_BY_FATEH.RawKEy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
